#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:164
msgid ""
"// List the unique IDs of a mount's strict descendants in the current\n"
"// mount namespace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:174
msgid "The `req` argument is a `struct mnt_id_req`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:175
msgid ""
"`mnt_id` is the parent mount's `unique_id`, or `LSMT_ROOT` (`(uint64_t)-1`) "
"for the current namespace's root mount."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:177
msgid ""
"`param` is a pagination cursor; only descendants with `unique_id` strictly "
"greater than `param` are returned (strictly less than `param` when "
"`LISTMOUNT_REVERSE` is set)."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:180
msgid ""
"`size` must equal `MNT_ID_REQ_SIZE_VER0` (24); future struct versions are "
"not yet accepted."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:182
msgid "`spare` must be `0`."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:184
msgid "Limitations:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/syscall-flag-coverage/file-systems-and-mount-control/index.md:185
msgid ""
"Bind-mount visibility filtering (Linux's `is_path_reachable`) is not yet "
"modeled; descendancy is determined by the strict mount parent chain."
msgstr ""

